# RELEASE — zsh-snap-rollback

Version:  v1.2
Date:     2026-04-12
Platform: openSUSE Tumbleweed
Shell:    zsh 5.9+

---

## What's in this release

### v1.2 — Auto sudo detection
- Detects if sudo is required for snapper — compatible with ALLOW_USERS/ALLOW_GROUPS

### v1.1 — Robust parsing + post-rollback check
- Replaced `│`-based parsing with `snapper --csvout` — locale-independent
- Post-rollback exit code verification — no false success message
- Fallback to `sudo snapper list` if snap-list plugin is absent

### v1.0 — Initial release
- Guided rollback flow: `snap-rollback` lists all snapshots, user picks a number
- Target snapshot summary: date, type, importance, description
- Double safety: explicit irreversibility warning + `[y/N]` confirmation
- Dry-run mode: `snap-rollback <id> --dry-run` simulates without executing
- Reboot reminder after rollback completion
- Depends on zsh-snap-list for the guided display
